    {
      "id": "winback-title",
      "name": "Title Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        -380
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# Run Win-Back Campaign\n\nHandler for the win-back event (event 'winback_run'): re-engages customers who have not ordered for a while, in two independent passes (first email; follow-up email, plus an SMS when there is a phone).\n\n**Called by:** the main workflow '[GHL Store Automation] | WF1 - Store Events & Win-Back' (its 'Run ... Handler' node, chosen by 'Route By Event Type'), which passes the normalised event together with the store settings. **Standalone-capable:** no.\n\n**Sections on this canvas:**\n1. Win-Back\n\nGoHighLevel work is done by the GHL Adapter workflow (mock or live, chosen by 'ghl_adapter_id') and email by the Email Sender workflow (both called with Execute Workflow). Any failure is reported to the central error handler with THIS workflow's name and the failed node's name.",
        "width": 3420,
        "height": 340,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "winback-sec",
      "name": "Section 1 Note - Win-Back",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Win-back\n\nTriggered by: the main workflow's 'Run ... Handler' node, event 'winback_run'.\n\nWhat it does, step by step:\n1. Stops immediately when winback_enabled is off (pause it without touching lead capture).\n2. PASS A - customers whose last order is older than winback_first_days and who are not already in a sequence (or finished one more than winback_cooldown_days ago): sends the win-back email, records 'email_sent', tags the contact 'winback-active'.\n3. PASS B - customers who got the email at least winback_sms_gap_days ago and have not ordered since: sends the follow-up email, plus an SMS when there is a phone, records 'done', tags the contact 'winback-sms-sent'.\n4. Customers are processed one by one. A customer who orders is reset by the Paid Order section.\n\nThe two passes run independently, so an empty pass A never blocks pass B.",
        "width": 3420,
        "height": 1280,
        "color": 2
      }
    }
